chived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2025-03-19T15:08:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T13:05:46Z","closed_at":"2025-04-04T22:17:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7270) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-6700K CPU @ 4.00GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf app starts with Vsync OFF (`display/window/vsync/vsync_mode == Disabled`), then on focus change the monitor will flicker. However, if user sets Vsync to ON and then to OFF again when app is running (using `DisplayServer.window_set_vsync_mode()`), the monitor will no longer flicker, even though the Vsync is OFF like it was in the beginning.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set Exclusive Fullscreen mode in the project settings\n2. Set Vsync Disabled in the project settings\n3. Run the app\n4. Switch to a different monitor or just use alt+tab/winkey\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[monitor-flickers-vsync-off.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19343540/monitor-flickers-vsync-off.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"ghuser404","id":33043976,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDQzOTc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33043976?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghuser404","html_url":"https://git